  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe five Fanuc-family posts now write each length word with a decimal point: `Z14.`, never `Z14`. Fanuc parameter 3401 bit 0 (DPI) sets how the control reads a word with no point. With DPI=0 the control reads `Z14` as 0.014 mm, and a rapid to it goes almost to Z0. With the point, DPI=0 and DPI=1 read the same value.\n\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`, `haas.cps`, `mazak.cps`, `doosan-dnm.cps`: a new helper `pt` adds the point. The length format `fu` and the angle format `fa` use it. The helper `fn` keeps the old trimmed text for comments and for macro-B expressions (a macro-B constant is not scaled by DPI).\n- `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`: the same for X (diameter), Z, I, K, R, the C angle, the feed per revolution and the thread lead (`F2.`), and the G76 R finish allowance. The G76 P/Q and G83 Q words stay in whole least increments: the control documents these addresses as \"no decimal point\".\n- Feeds per minute are not changed (`F300`, or in/min at two decimals).\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`: a new law bullet \"A length word carries its decimal point (#1836)\".\n- `docs/decisions/1836-fanuc-decimal-point.md`: the decision entry.\n\n## The golden changes\n\nAll golden diffs of the Fanuc-family posts add only a trailing `.` to whole-number length, angle, lead and feed-per-rev words (for example `G00 X10 Y0 Z5` becomes `G00 X10. Y0. Z5.`). No value changes. No block is added or removed. The probe macro lines (`IF[ABS[#5063-25]GT0.001]...`, `#190=#100+17`) do not change. The goldens of the other posts do not change.\n\n`crates/post/tests/explain_fanuc_family.rs` now writes its Explain golden when `WRITE_GOLDEN` is set, as the other golden tests do.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/post/tests/decimal_point_fanuc_family.rs`:\n- `the_mill_posts_write_a_whole_number_length_with_its_point` (fanuc, haas, mazak, doosan-dnm: `Z14.`, `Z-8.`, `X30.`, and no motion word with a bare length)\n- `the_mill_posts_write_a_whole_number_inch_length_with_its_point` (the same four posts in inch: `Z1.`, `Z-1.`)\n- `the_lathe_post_writes_a_whole_number_length_and_feed_per_rev_with_its_point` (fanuc-lathe: `X30. Z14.`, `Z-8.`, `F1.`)\n\nThe existing tests with inline G-code text of these posts now expect the point.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post`: all test binaries pass, with the new `decimal_point_fanuc_family` tests.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app` on the touched binaries: all pass. The full app suite was also run one time. Only `sodick_alc400g` fails, and it fails on main too (#1856, the fix is on PR #1857).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- A script compared each changed golden with main: each diff only adds a `.` after a whole-number word.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- No real control was run with DPI=0 or DPI=1. The behaviour comes from the published parameter documentation.\n- The feed-per-minute format and the non-Fanuc posts (Sinumerik, Heidenhain, Tormach, grblHAL, TinyG, Carvera) are not changed and not examined again.\n- The release-tier heavy lanes and the pixel snapshots were not run.\n\nChangelog: Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM and Fanuc lathe posts now write each whole-number length, angle and feed-per-revolution word with a decimal point (`Z14.`), so that a control with parameter 3401#0 DPI=0 does not read it in least increments (#1836).\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1836\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
